---
description: 2–3 letter acronyms ID, HP, NPC, URL, UTC. Never Id, Hp, Npc, Url, Utc. Not units.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Naming

Only `ID`, `HP`, `NPC`, `URL`, `UTC`. Not HTTP, JSON, or units: casing there is meaning (`Mb` ≠ `MB`, `Ms` ≠ `MS`).

Never `Id`, `Hp`, `Npc`, `Url`, `Utc`. PascalCase: `NPCDirector`. camelCase: `npcID`, `fromURL`. Whole name: `id`, `hp`, `npc`, `url`, `utc`.

Timestamps: game time fields/variables are named `timestamp` or `*Timestamp`. UTC fields/variables end with `UTC` (`savedUTC`). Never `At`.

No leading or trailing `_` on names (`no-underscore-dangle`). Privacy is the `private` keyword, not a prefix.
